      "title": "Gender-diverse Australian sailors barred from US submarines despite Aukus deal, documents reveal",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/gender-diverse-australian-sailors-barred-from-us-submarines-despite-aukus-deal-documents-reveal-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Defence briefing released under freedom of information laws shows ADF beholden to US directives when in training</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Aukus is effectively forcing the Australian navy to comply with a US ban on transgender people in the military with gender-diverse navy recruits <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jun/01/transgender-troops-military-enlistment-ruling\">prevented from starting a career</a> in nuclear submarines because they would not be safe training on US boats.</p><p>Internal Australian defence force documents show transgender and non-binary sailors and officers are explicitly banned from Australia’s nuclear submarine training program because of US policies..</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/gender-diverse-australian-sailors-barred-from-us-submarines-despite-aukus-deal-documents-reveal-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T14:00:19"
    },
    {
      "title": "Anthony Albanese apologises for hot-mic gaffe after Coalition criticises ‘locker-room talk’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/anthony-albanese-apologises-for-hot-mic-gaffe-after-coalition-criticises-locker-room-talk",
      "description": "<p>Prime minister says he and Chris Bowen were having ‘light-hearted banter’ when they were caught discussing where they keep their phones</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Anthony Albanese has apologised for a hot-mic gaffe at the UN climate talks in Turkey, saying he regretted being overheard discussing mobile phone radiation and “dicks” in a candid conversation.</p><p>“I of course regret that. I apologise,” Albanese said during a visit to the Australian warship HMAS Stalwart in the Philippines on Sunday.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/anthony-albanese-apologises-for-hot-mic-gaffe-after-coalition-criticises-locker-room-talk\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
